# How to cite this software (GitHub's "Cite this repository"; read by Zenodo at a release). The authors below
# are the software's; the paper, with its own authors, is the preferred citation (its journal, year and DOI to
# come).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below (its full citation is to come) and the software."
type: software
title: "ASTRID: astrocyte-informed demixing of neuronal calcium traces"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT    # except the folders reproduce/tuncat_eval/ and reproduce/tuncat_peers/, GPL-2.0-only (README.md)
repository-code: "https://github.com/jameschengpeng/ASTRID"
keywords:
  - calcium imaging
  - demixing
  - astrocytes
  - neuropil
  - two-photon
  - one-photon
abstract: >-
  ASTRID (ASTRocyte-Informed Demixing) demixes the calcium traces of neuronal ROIs in imaging where neurons
  and astrocytes share one fluorescence channel. For each ROI, it fits a model of the patch of pixels around
  it, with the neuron's own signal, the neighboring neurons, astrocyte components placed on astrocyte
  territory, and the local neuropil.
authors:
